---
layout: base.njk
description: "Jason Figueroa is a software engineer working in C# and .NET, with experience in enterprise applications, production troubleshooting, and modernization."
---
<section class="intro">
  <p class="eyebrow">Software engineering · .NET</p>
  <h1>Useful software.<br>Carefully built.</h1>
  <p class="lead">I’m Jason, a software engineer working in C# and .NET. I untangle complex applications, troubleshoot production problems, and help existing systems evolve.</p>
  <p class="muted">This is where I keep notes on the things I build, maintain, and figure out along the way.</p>
  <a href="/about/">More about my work →</a>
</section>
<section class="ruled-section" aria-labelledby="writing-heading">
  <h2 class="eyebrow" id="writing-heading">From the notebook</h2>
  {% for article in collections.articles %}{% if loop.first %}
  <article class="article-listing">
    <h3><a href="{{ article.url }}">{{ article.data.title }}</a></h3>
    <p class="muted">{{ article.data.description }}</p>
    <p class="article-meta">{{ article.data.category }} · <time datetime="{{ article.date | isoDate }}">{{ article.date | readableDate }}</time></p>
  </article>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
</section>
<section class="ruled-section" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
  <h2 id="approach-heading">How I approach the work</h2>
  <p>I’m comfortable starting with an unfamiliar codebase and incomplete documentation. I follow the behavior through the system, work out what needs to change, and see the fix through.</p>
  <ul class="focus-list"><li>Understand the existing system</li><li>Make focused changes</li><li>Verify the result</li></ul>
</section>
